// =============================================================================
// LAKEFLOW CONNECT DIRECT CDC FROM ON-PREMISES ON GCP: PRIVATE SERVICE CONNECT
//
// JSONC for you to read; emit PLAIN JSON (strip the // lines) when you write
// architecture.md. Read reference/style-networking.md first.
//
// HOW IT WORKS ON DATABRICKS (use this to adapt the diagram to the user's network):
//   • Lakeflow Connect Direct CDC: ONE scheduled serverless pipeline does the snapshot,
//     the change data capture and the replication. There is no separate ingestion
//     gateway to run. Private Preview, SQL Server and Oracle only; during the preview the
//     connection to an on-prem database may have to be created in SQL, not in the UI.
//   • The pipeline runs on serverless, outside the customer's VPC, so it needs a private
//     path to the database. On Azure and AWS that path is a Private Network Gateway; on
//     GCP it is the Private Service Connect chain of serverless-psc-gcp.jsonc, built by
//     the customer in the hub VPC:
//       1. a Hybrid Connectivity NEG with the database's private IP and port as endpoints;
//       2. an internal TCP Proxy Load Balancer using the NEG as backend, its Envoy proxies
//          in a regional proxy-only subnet advertised to on-prem over BGP (Cloud Router);
//       3. a PSC service attachment fronting the forwarding rule (dedicated NAT subnet);
//       4. a private endpoint rule in the workspace's NCC targeting that attachment.
//   • The hub reaches on-prem over Cloud Interconnect or HA VPN. The workspace VPC is
//     peered to the hub and is not on the pipeline's path.
//
// WHAT IT DEMONSTRATES (layout): the serverless-psc-gcp shape with a different source and
// targets. The source is the Lakeflow Connect pipeline (not generic serverless), the
// targets are the two supported databases, and the preview status sits in the frame
// subtitle instead of a floating badge.
//
// ADAPT IT: on Azure / AWS replace the hub chain with a PNG subnet (see
// serverless-png-azure.jsonc). When no connection into the data centre is allowed at all,
// that is the Lakeflow Connect on-prem agent, not this path.
// =============================================================================
